 ENDF/B-VI.8 MF32 rel uncertainties adjusted to the those from    1125 1451   31
 the Atlas of Neutron Resonances [1]. Thermal uncertainties for   1125 1451   32
 capture and elastic were added using file 33. Elastic was set    1125 1451   33
 to 5.5%, as half the difference between the thermal value in     1125 1451   34
 this evaluation and the value in the Atlas. The capture thermal  1125 1451   35
 unc was taken from the Atlas.                                    1125 1451   36
                                                                  1125 1451   37
 In the fast neutron region the sensitivity calculations were     1125 1451   38
 performed with the EMPIRE code. The spherical optical model      1125 1451   39
 provided total cross sections and neutron scattering,            1125 1451   40
 Hauser-Feshbach statistical model described the bulk of particle 1125 1451   41
 emission, and the exciton pre-equilibrium model described major  1125 1451   42
 features of fast particle emission at higher incident energies.  1125 1451   43
 Altogether, 21 model parameters were varied. The Bayesian        1125 1451   44
 update procedure was performed by the KALMAN [2] code by taking  1125 1451   45
 into account the sensitivity calculations and selected           1125 1451   46
 experimental data.                                               1125 1451   47
                                                                  1125 1451   48
[1] S. F. Mughabghab, "Atlas of Neutron Resonances: Thermal       1125 1451   49
    Cross Sections and Resonance Parameters", Elsevier,           1125 1451   50
    Amsterdam, 2006.                                              1125 1451   51
[2] D. Rochman, M. Herman, P. Oblozinsky, and S. F. Mughabghab,   1125 1451   52
    "Preliminary Cross Section Covariances for WPEC Subgroup 26," 1125 1451   53
    Rep. BNL-77407-2007-IR, Brookhaven National Laboratory (2007) 1125 1451   54
                                                                  1125 1451   55
