 ENDF/B-V Evaluation, December 1977, D. C. Larson (ORNL)          1125 1451   83
                                                                  1125 1451   84
MF=2                                                              1125 1451   85
   Resonance parameters are used from 600 eV to 500 keV.  The     1125 1451   86
 thermal capture cross section is given as 528 mb, in agreement   1125 1451   87
 with the experimental results of 526.9+-4.5 mb [RY71], as well   1125 1451   88
 as earlier results summarized in [RY71].  Using resonance        1125 1451   89
 parameters E=2.81 keV, GN=376 eV, and GG=0.353 eV for the large  1125 1451   90
 2.81 keV resonance gives the correct thermal capture value using 1125 1451   91
 a Breit-Wigner shape, and this form is used to calculate the     1125 1451   92
 capture crposs section from 1.0E-5 to 600 eV.  The capture       1125 1451   93
 width GG=0.353 eV is consistent with a recent result by Wilson   1125 1451   94
 [WI77] where they find 0.24<GG<0.4 eV with a 90% confidence      1125 1451   95
 level, and with a recent preliminary result of Macklin [MA76]    1125 1451   96
 where he found GG=0.385+-0.04 eV.  The GN and ER values are      1125 1451   97
 taken from Seltzer [SE74].  From 600 eV to 500 keV, the capture  1125 1451   98
 cross section is generated from resonance areas reported by      1125 1451   99
 Musgrove [MU77], and neutron widths and spins obtained from      1125 1451  100
 a multilevel analysis of the transmission data of Larson [LA76]. 1125 1451  101
                                                                  1125 1451  102
MF=3                                                              1125 1451  103
   MT=1  Resonance parameters + data of Larson [LA76].            1125 1451  104
   MT=2  MT=1 - MT=3                                              1125 1451  105
   MT=3  SUM 3/4+3/16+3/102+3/103+3/107                           1125 1451  106
   MT=4  SUM 3/51-68,91                                           1125 1451  107
   MT=102  As discussed above, the shape of the capture cross     1125 1451  108
     section from 1.E-5 eV to 600 eV was taken from a single      1125 1451  109
     level Breit-Wigner form from 600 eV to 500 keV, File 3 gives 1125 1451  110
     no contribution.  From 500 keV to 20 MeV the capture file is 1125 1451  111
     the same as the ENDF/B-IV file by Pitterle and Paik [PI72].  1125 1451  112
   MT=103  Taken from ENDF4 - Modified >8 MeV                     1125 1451  113
     Based on 2 step Hauser-Feshbach calculations                 1125 1451  114
   MT=107  Taken from ENDF/B-IV                                   1125 1451  115
MF=4                                                              1125 1451  116
   MT=2  Taken mainly from [KI76], ENDF/B-IV and Optical Model    1125 1451  117
     calculations. All other angular distributions assumed        1125 1451  118
     isotropic.                                                   1125 1451  119
MF=5                                                              1125 1451  120
   MT=16  Taken from ENDF/B-IV.                                   1125 1451  121
   MT=91  Temperatures adjusted to fit neutron production         1125 1451  122
         data of Hermsdorf [HE75].                                1125 1451  123
MF=8                                                              1125 1451  124
   Data from Reich and Endt and from Vander Leun                  1125 1451  125
MF=12                                                             1125 1451  126
   MT=102  Data taken from ENDF/B-IV.                             1125 1451  127
MF=13                                                             1125 1451  128
   MT=3  n,xgamma data from [LA77].                               1125 1451  129
MF=14                                                             1125 1451  130
   All angular distributions assumed isotropic.                   1125 1451  131
MF=15                                                             1125 1451  132
